1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,760
When a knowledge graph says two ideas are related, the link is only as useful as its evidence.

2
00:00:06,340 --> 00:00:08,760
A good graph keeps three things together.

3
00:00:09,260 --> 00:00:15,160
The claim, the exact passage at support, and the finger print of the source file.

4
00:00:15,940 --> 00:00:17,380
Translation at the other layer.

5
00:00:17,920 --> 00:00:25,200
The original phrase, the translated phrase, and the translators uncertainty should stay visible side by side.

6
00:00:25,200 --> 00:00:27,240
This makes correction easier.

7
00:00:27,600 --> 00:00:34,900
A reader can follow the link back to the passage, check the wording, and decide whether the relationship still holds.

8
00:00:35,580 --> 00:00:40,420
Provens does not make every claim true, but it makes each claim impeccable.

